  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>&nbsp;be the set of all the natural numbers, for which the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;is a tangent to the curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then",
    "image": null
  },
